course: dictionary
lesson: 12535
title: Detachable: parts that come off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some things are made in parts that can be taken off and fitted back on. The word for this is detachable. Detachable means able to be removed and put back again. «My jumper has a detachable hood, so I can take it off when I get hot.» The hood comes off, and it can go back on later.
explain: Look at the word's parts. Detach means to take something off, and attach means to fix something on. Detachable is what you call a thing that can be detached. If you can unclip it, unscrew it or unzip it and then put it back, it is detachable.
explain: Detachable is an adjective. It tells you about a noun, like hood, keyboard or strap. Use the words around it as clues. «The keyboard is detachable, so Sam can take it off the tablet.» The sentence tells you the keyboard comes off, so detachable must mean it can be removed.
fact: Detachable means able to be removed and put back again.
fact: Detach means to take something off, and attach means to fix something on.
fact: Detachable is an adjective, so it describes a thing, such as a detachable collar.
fact: «Detachable» is used about clothes and things: a detachable hood, a detachable collar, a detachable keyboard or a detachable shower head.
fact: Detachable tells you the part comes off and can be fitted again, so the thing still works as one whole.
exercise: «My jumper has a detachable hood, so I can take it off when I get hot.» What does detachable mean? | Always stuck on and never moves | *Able to be removed and put back | Made of soft wool | Very warm and thick
exercise: «The keyboard is detachable, so Sam can take it off the tablet.» What does detachable mean here? | Broken and no longer working | Glowing in the dark | Tiny and light | *Can be removed from the tablet
exercise: Which word means to fix something on again? | Detach | *Attach | Remove | Lift
test: «Mum cleaned the detachable shower head.» What does detachable tell you about the shower head? | It is made of glass | *It can be taken off and put back | It is always hot | It cannot be moved at all
test: Ella's school bag has a detachable strap. What does this tell you? | *The strap can be removed and fitted back on | The strap is glued on for ever | The strap is made of paper | The strap is bigger than the bag
exam: Which thing is detachable? | *A hood that zips off and can be put back on | A tree with deep roots | A river that never stops moving | A solid wall built of bricks
